/-!
# Ch. 0 §2 (p. 127): the existence of blowing-up for `(ℛ/S)`-ideals, by annihilators

> However, the existence of blowing-up in the category 𝓜(ℛ/S) implies the same in the category 𝒥(ℛ/S). In fact, let
> M = (X, J) be an (ℛ/S)-ideal with X = (X, O_X). Let (N, Φ) be a blowing-up of M in the category 𝓜(ℛ/S) with
> N = (P, I), P = (P, O_P), and with Φ = (f, φ), f = (f, θ). Let H be the union of the annihilators of θ(J)ⁿ in O_P
> for all positive integers n. Let P′ be the support of O_P/H, O_{P′} the restriction of O_P/H to P′ and
> P′ = (P′, O_{P′}). Let I′ be the sheaf of ideals in O_{P′} which is generated by the natural image of θ(J). Then Φ
> induces a natural morphism Φ′: (P′, I′) → (X, J), which is a morphism of (ℛ/S)-ideals. It can be easily seen that
> (N′, Φ′) with N′ = (P′, I′) is a blowing-up of M in the category 𝒥(ℛ/S). Thus we obtain the exitence [sic] theorem of
> blowing-up in the category 𝒥(ℛ/S), where S is any local-ringed space or a commutative ring with unity. (p. 127)

## What is formalized

The construction as printed, for an `(ℛ/S)`-ideal `M = (X, J)` (`RIdealOver S`) and a morphism `Φ = (f, φ)` of
`(ℛ/S)`-modules from `N = (P, I)` to `M` viewed as a module (`RIdealOver.asModuleOver`):

* `RIdeal.annihilatorUnion`, `RIdeal.annihilatorFamily`: the sheaf `H`, the union of the annihilators in `O_P` of the
  powers of the ideal generated by `θ(J)`, as the family of ideals `H(U) ⊆ O_P(U)`;
* `AnnihilatorConstruction.support` (`P′`, with `O_{P′}` the restriction of `O_P/H` to the support of `O_P/H`),
  `supportIncl` (the morphism `P′ → P`), `ideal` (`I′`), `object` (`(P′, I′)` over `S`) and `hom` (`Φ′`, a morphism of
  `(ℛ/S)`-ideals `(P′, I′) → (X, J)`);
* the claim that `(N′, Φ′)` is a blowing-up of `M` in `𝒥(ℛ/S)`, as a `def … : Prop` (`AnnihilatorConstructionIsBlowingUp`).

## Formalization notes (encoding)

* `θ(J)ⁿ`: `θ(J)` is the image of `J` under `θ : O_X → f_*O_P`; its `n`-th power generates the same ideal of `O_P` as
  the `n`-th power of the sheaf of ideals `θ(J)O_P = f⁻¹(J)` (p. 128; `RIdeal.pullbackIdeal`).  The annihilator of the
  `n`-th power over an open `U` is the set of sections `s ∈ O_P(U)` with `s|_V · a₁ ⋯ aₙ = 0` for all open `V ⊆ U` and all
  sections `aᵢ ∈ f⁻¹(J)(V)` (`RIdeal.annihilatorPower`).
* "The union ... for all positive integers `n`": the union as a sheaf, i.e. `s` is a section of `H` over `U` if every point
  of `U` has an open neighbourhood `V ⊆ U` and an `n ≥ 1` with `s|_V` in the annihilator of the `n`-th power over `V`
  (`RIdeal.annihilatorUnion`).  For a quasi-compact `U` this is the union of the presheaf annihilators.
* `O_P/H` is the sheafification of the presheaf of rings `U ↦ O_P(U)/H(U)` (`IdealQuotient.quotientSheaf`); its support is
  the set of points where the stalk is non-zero (`IdealQuotient.supportSet`); `O_{P′}` is the restriction of this sheaf of
  rings to the support, i.e. the inverse image sheaf on the subspace (`SheafedSpace.restrictSubset`).  The paper writes
  `P′ = (P′, O_{P′})` and treats it as a local-ringed space: the stalks of `O_{P′}` are quotients of the local rings
  `O_{P,t}` that are non-zero, hence local, and `P′ → P` is a morphism of local-ringed spaces (a tacit step, proved:
  `IdealQuotient.isLocalRing_quotient_stalk`, `IdealQuotient.supportHom`).
* `Φ′` is "induced by `Φ`" through the underlying morphism of spaces `f ∘ j`, `j : P′ → P` the canonical morphism; `I′` is the
  sheaf of ideals generated by the image of `θ(J)` under `f ∘ j`, that is `(f ∘ j)⁻¹(J)` in the notation of p. 128.  Only `f` is
  used, not `φ`.  `(P′, I′)` is over `S` through `P′ → P → S`, and `Φ′` is a morphism over `S` (the `S`-structure of `N` and the
  condition that `Φ` is a morphism over `S`).  That `Φ′` is a morphism of `(ℛ/S)`-ideals ("which is a morphism of
  `(ℛ/S)`-ideals") holds by construction of `RIdeal.pullbackIdealHom`.

## Misprints of the source

p. 127 "exitence" (for "existence"), "dlowing-up" (for "blowing-up") in the preceding paragraph; the quotation above has
[sic] on the first.
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite AlgebraicGeometry TopCat

noncomputable section

universe u

namespace Hironaka

namespace IdealQuotient

/-! ### The quotient of a sheaf of rings by a family of ideals, its support and its restriction

Infrastructure for `O_P/H`, the support of `O_P/H` and `O_{P′}`.  No claim of the paper is proved here. -/

variable (P : SheafedSpace CommRingCat.{u})

/-- A family of ideals `H(U) ⊆ O_P(U)` compatible with restriction (the sections of a sheaf of ideals, or of a
subpresheaf of ideals, of the structure sheaf). -/
structure IdealFamily where
  /-- The ideal `H(U)` of `O_P(U)`. -/
  ideal : ∀ U : (Opens P)ᵒᵖ, Ideal (P.presheaf.obj U)
  /-- Restriction maps `H(U)` into `H(V)`. -/
  le_comap : ∀ {U V : (Opens P)ᵒᵖ} (i : U ⟶ V), ideal U ≤ (ideal V).comap (P.presheaf.map i).hom

variable {P}
variable (H : IdealFamily P)

/-- The presheaf of rings `U ↦ O_P(U)/H(U)`. -/
def quotientPresheaf : (Opens P)ᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{u} where
  obj U := CommRingCat.of (P.presheaf.obj U ⧸ H.ideal U)
  map {U V} i :=
    CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.quotientMap (H.ideal V) (P.presheaf.map i).hom (H.le_comap i))
  map_id U := by
    ext x
    simp
  map_comp {U V W} i j := by
    ext x
    simp

/-- The quotient maps `O_P(U) → O_P(U)/H(U)`, as a morphism of presheaves. -/
def toQuotientPresheaf : P.presheaf ⟶ quotientPresheaf H where
  app U := CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (H.ideal U))
  naturality {U V} i := by
    ext x
    exact congrArg (fun f => f x) (Ideal.quotientMap_comp_mk (H.le_comap i)).symm

/-- The sheaf of rings `O_P/H`: the sheafification of the presheaf quotient. -/
abbrev quotientSheaf : Sheaf CommRingCat.{u} P.carrier :=
  (presheafToSheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology P.carrier) CommRingCat.{u}).obj (quotientPresheaf H)

/-- The ringed space `(P, O_P/H)`. -/
abbrev quotientSpace : SheafedSpace CommRingCat.{u} where
  carrier := P.carrier
  presheaf := (quotientSheaf H).obj
  IsSheaf := (quotientSheaf H).property

/-- The morphism of ringed spaces `(P, O_P/H) ⟶ P` (the identity on spaces, the quotient map on sheaves). -/
def quotientHom : (quotientSpace H).toPresheafedSpace ⟶ P.toPresheafedSpace where
  base := 𝟙 _
  c := toQuotientPresheaf H ≫
    CategoryTheory.toSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology P.carrier) (quotientPresheaf H)

/-- The stalk maps of `(P, O_P/H) ⟶ P` are surjective: the stalk of `O_P/H` is a quotient of that of `O_P`. -/
lemma quotientHom_stalkMap_surjective (t : P) :
    Function.Surjective ((quotientHom H).stalkMap t).hom := by
  intro y
  obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ : ∃ z, ((Presheaf.stalkFunctor CommRingCat.{u} t).map
      (CategoryTheory.toSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology P.carrier)
        (quotientPresheaf H))).hom z = y := by
    have : IsIso ((Presheaf.stalkFunctor CommRingCat.{u} t).map
      (CategoryTheory.toSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology P.carrier) (quotientPresheaf H))) :=
      Presheaf.stalkFunctor_map_unit_toSheafify_isIso t CommRingCat.{u} (quotientPresheaf H)
    exact (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso ((Presheaf.stalkFunctor CommRingCat.{u} t).map
      (CategoryTheory.toSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology P.carrier)
        (quotientPresheaf H)))).2 y
  obtain ⟨U, hU, a, rfl⟩ := Presheaf.exists_germ_eq (quotientPresheaf H) z
  obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective a
  refine ⟨P.presheaf.germ U t hU a, ?_⟩
  erw [PresheafedSpace.stalkMap_germ_apply (quotientHom H) U t hU a]
  erw [Presheaf.stalkFunctor_map_germ_apply]
  rfl

section Local

variable {P : LocallyRingedSpace.{u}} (H : IdealFamily P.toSheafedSpace)

/-- The support of `O_P/H`: the points where the stalk of `O_P/H` is not the zero ring.

> Let P′ be the support of O_P/H ... (p. 127) -/
def supportSet : Set P := {t | Nontrivial ((quotientSpace H).presheaf.stalk t)}

/-- At a point of the support, the stalk of `O_P/H` is a local ring: it is a non-zero quotient of the local ring
`O_{P,t}`.  This is the tacit step by which `P′ = (P′, O_{P′})` is a local-ringed space. -/
lemma isLocalRing_quotient_stalk (t : supportSet H) :
    IsLocalRing ((quotientSpace H).presheaf.stalk (t : P)) := by
  have : Nontrivial ((quotientSpace H).presheaf.stalk (t : P)) := t.2
  exact IsLocalRing.of_surjective' ((quotientHom H).stalkMap (t : P)).hom
    (quotientHom_stalkMap_surjective H (t : P))

/-- The local-ringed space `P′ = (P′, O_{P′})`: the support of `O_P/H` with the restriction of `O_P/H` to it.

> ... O_{P′} the restriction of O_P/H to P′ and P′ = (P′, O_{P′}). (p. 127) -/
def supportSpace : LocallyRingedSpace.{u} :=
  (quotientSpace H).restrictSubsetLocallyRingedSpace (supportSet H) (isLocalRing_quotient_stalk H)

lemma restrictSubsetHom_comp_stalkMap_surjective (Y : SheafedSpace CommRingCat.{u}) (T : Set Y)
    (α : Y.toPresheafedSpace ⟶ P.toPresheafedSpace) (t : Y.subspace T)
    (h : Function.Surjective (α.stalkMap (Y.subspaceIncl T t)).hom) :
    Function.Surjective ((Y.restrictSubsetHom T ≫ α).stalkMap t).hom := by
  erw [PresheafedSpace.stalkMap.comp]
  exact (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso ((Y.restrictSubsetHom T).stalkMap t)).2.comp h

/-- The canonical morphism `P′ ⟶ P` of local-ringed spaces: the restriction to the support followed by the quotient
map.  Its stalk maps are surjective ring homomorphisms between local rings, hence local. -/
def supportHom : supportSpace H ⟶ P :=
  ⟨(quotientSpace H).restrictSubsetHom (supportSet H) ≫ quotientHom H, fun t => by
    let t' : (quotientSpace H).subspace (supportSet H) := t
    have hsurj := restrictSubsetHom_comp_stalkMap_surjective (quotientSpace H) (supportSet H)
      (quotientHom H) t' (quotientHom_stalkMap_surjective H _)
    have : Nontrivial ((supportSpace H).presheaf.stalk t) := by
      have : Nontrivial ((quotientSpace H).presheaf.stalk
          ((quotientSpace H).subspaceIncl _ t')) := t'.2
      exact ((quotientSpace H).restrictSubsetStalkIso (supportSet H) t').commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.toEquiv.nontrivial
    exact IsLocalHom.of_surjective _ hsurj⟩

end Local

end IdealQuotient

open IdealQuotient

/-! ### The annihilators of the powers of an ideal, and their union -/

variable (𝔞 : RIdeal.{u})

/-- The image in `O_X(V)` of a section of the sheaf of ideals `𝔞` over `V`. -/
def RIdeal.toSection {V : Opens 𝔞.X} (a : 𝔞.J.val.obj (op V)) : 𝔞.X.presheaf.obj (op V) :=
  (𝔞.ι.val.app (op V)).hom a

lemma presheaf_map_map {X : SheafedSpace CommRingCat.{u}} {U V W : Opens X} (hVU : V ≤ U)
    (hWV : W ≤ V) (s : X.presheaf.obj (op U)) :
    (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWV).op).hom ((X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op).hom s) =
      (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hWV.trans hVU)).op).hom s := by
  rw [← CommRingCat.comp_apply, ← X.presheaf.map_comp]
  rfl

/-- The annihilator over `U` of the `n`-th power of the sheaf of ideals `𝔞` in `O_X`: the sections `s ∈ O_X(U)` with
`s|_V · a₁ ⋯ aₙ = 0` for all open `V ⊆ U` and all sections `a₁, …, aₙ` of `𝔞` over `V`.  See the module docstring. -/
def RIdeal.annihilatorPower (n : ℕ) (U : Opens 𝔞.X) : Set (𝔞.X.presheaf.obj (op U)) :=
  {s | ∀ (V : Opens 𝔞.X) (hV : V ≤ U) (a : Fin n → 𝔞.J.val.obj (op V)),
    (𝔞.X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hV).op).hom s * ∏ i, 𝔞.toSection (a i) = 0}

lemma RIdeal.annihilatorPower_restrict {n : ℕ} {U V : Opens 𝔞.X} (hVU : V ≤ U)
    {s : 𝔞.X.presheaf.obj (op U)} (hs : s ∈ 𝔞.annihilatorPower n U) :
    (𝔞.X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op).hom s ∈ 𝔞.annihilatorPower n V := by
  intro W hW a
  rw [presheaf_map_map]
  exact hs W (hW.trans hVU) a

lemma RIdeal.annihilatorPower_mono {n : ℕ} {U : Opens 𝔞.X} {s : 𝔞.X.presheaf.obj (op U)}
    (hs : s ∈ 𝔞.annihilatorPower n U) : s ∈ 𝔞.annihilatorPower (n + 1) U := by
  intro V hV a
  rw [Fin.prod_univ_castSucc, ← mul_assoc, hs V hV (fun i => a i.castSucc), zero_mul]

lemma RIdeal.annihilatorPower_mono' {m n : ℕ} (h : m ≤ n) {U : Opens 𝔞.X}
    {s : 𝔞.X.presheaf.obj (op U)} (hs : s ∈ 𝔞.annihilatorPower m U) :
    s ∈ 𝔞.annihilatorPower n U := by
  induction h with
  | refl => exact hs
  | step _ ih => exact 𝔞.annihilatorPower_mono ih

lemma RIdeal.annihilatorPower_add {n : ℕ} {U : Opens 𝔞.X} {s t : 𝔞.X.presheaf.obj (op U)}
    (hs : s ∈ 𝔞.annihilatorPower n U) (ht : t ∈ 𝔞.annihilatorPower n U) :
    s + t ∈ 𝔞.annihilatorPower n U := by
  intro V hV a
  rw [map_add, add_mul, hs V hV a, ht V hV a, add_zero]

lemma RIdeal.annihilatorPower_smul {n : ℕ} {U : Opens 𝔞.X} (r s : 𝔞.X.presheaf.obj (op U))
    (hs : s ∈ 𝔞.annihilatorPower n U) : r * s ∈ 𝔞.annihilatorPower n U := by
  intro V hV a
  rw [map_mul, mul_assoc, hs V hV a, mul_zero]

/-- The sections over `U` of `H`, the union of the annihilators of the powers of `𝔞` in `O_X` for all positive integers
`n` (as a sheaf: locally in the annihilator of some power).

> Let H be the union of the annihilators of θ(J)ⁿ in O_P for all positive integers n. (p. 127)

Definition (p. 127).  Formalization notes (encoding): see the module docstring (`θ(J)ⁿ` is read through the ideal
`θ(J)O_P`, the union is the sheaf union). -/
def RIdeal.annihilatorUnion (U : Opens 𝔞.X) : Set (𝔞.X.presheaf.obj (op U)) :=
  {s | ∀ x ∈ U, ∃ (V : Opens 𝔞.X) (hV : V ≤ U), x ∈ V ∧ ∃ n : ℕ, 0 < n ∧
    (𝔞.X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hV).op).hom s ∈ 𝔞.annihilatorPower n V}

/-- `RIdeal.annihilatorUnion` is an ideal of `O_X(U)`. -/
def RIdeal.annihilatorUnionIdeal (U : Opens 𝔞.X) : Ideal (𝔞.X.presheaf.obj (op U)) where
  carrier := 𝔞.annihilatorUnion U
  zero_mem' := by
    intro x hx
    refine ⟨U, le_rfl, hx, 1, one_pos, ?_⟩
    intro W hW a
    simp
  add_mem' := by
    intro s t hs ht x hx
    obtain ⟨V₁, h₁, hx₁, n₁, hn₁, hs₁⟩ := hs x hx
    obtain ⟨V₂, h₂, hx₂, n₂, hn₂, ht₂⟩ := ht x hx
    refine ⟨V₁ ⊓ V₂, inf_le_left.trans h₁, ⟨hx₁, hx₂⟩, max n₁ n₂, lt_max_of_lt_left hn₁, ?_⟩
    have e1 := 𝔞.annihilatorPower_restrict (inf_le_left : V₁ ⊓ V₂ ≤ V₁) hs₁
    have e2 := 𝔞.annihilatorPower_restrict (inf_le_right : V₁ ⊓ V₂ ≤ V₂) ht₂
    rw [presheaf_map_map] at e1 e2
    have e1' := 𝔞.annihilatorPower_mono' (le_max_left n₁ n₂) e1
    have e2' := 𝔞.annihilatorPower_mono' (le_max_right n₁ n₂) e2
    have := 𝔞.annihilatorPower_add e1' e2'
    rwa [← map_add] at this
  smul_mem' := by
    intro r s hs x hx
    obtain ⟨V, h, hxV, n, hn, hs'⟩ := hs x hx
    refine ⟨V, h, hxV, n, hn, ?_⟩
    have := 𝔞.annihilatorPower_smul ((𝔞.X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op).hom r) _ hs'
    simpa [smul_eq_mul, map_mul] using this

/-- The family of ideals `H(U)`: the union of the annihilators of the powers of `𝔞`. -/
def RIdeal.annihilatorFamily : IdealFamily 𝔞.X.toSheafedSpace where
  ideal U := 𝔞.annihilatorUnionIdeal U.unop
  le_comap {U V} i s hs := by
    intro x hx
    obtain ⟨W, hW, hxW, n, hn, hs'⟩ := hs x (i.unop.le hx)
    refine ⟨W ⊓ V.unop, inf_le_right, ⟨hxW, hx⟩, n, hn, ?_⟩
    have := 𝔞.annihilatorPower_restrict (inf_le_left : W ⊓ V.unop ≤ W) hs'
    rw [presheaf_map_map] at this
    rw [show i = (homOfLE i.unop.le).op from rfl, presheaf_map_map]
    exact this

/-! ### The morphism of ideals induced by a morphism of spaces -/

/-- The canonical morphism `(X′, f⁻¹(J)) ⟶ (X, J)` of `ℛ`-ideals over a morphism `g : X′ ⟶ X`: `g` with the canonical
`g`-epimorphism of `J` onto `θ(J)O_{X′}`, compatible with the monomorphisms.  This is the content of "which is a
morphism of `(ℛ/S)`-ideals" (p. 127) and of "the morphism of `ℛ`-ideals is `(f, φ)` with the canonical `f`-epimorphism
`φ` of `J₂` to `θ(J₂)O_{X₁}`" (p. 128). -/
def RIdeal.pullbackIdealHom (I : RIdeal.{u}) {X' : LocallyRingedSpace.{u}} (g : X' ⟶ I.X) :
    I.pullbackIdeal g ⟶ I where
  toHom := ⟨g, Abelian.factorThruImage ((OModules.pullback g).map I.ι ≫ OModules.pullbackUnitToUnit g),
    (inferInstance : Epi (Abelian.factorThruImage
      ((OModules.pullback g).map I.ι ≫ OModules.pullbackUnitToUnit g)))⟩
  compat := (Abelian.image.fac ((OModules.pullback g).map I.ι ≫ OModules.pullbackUnitToUnit g)).symm

variable {S : LocallyRingedSpace.{u}}

/-- An `(ℛ/S)`-ideal `M = (X, J)` viewed as an `(ℛ/S)`-module "in a natural way" (p. 127). -/
def RIdealOver.asModuleOver (I : RIdealOver S) : RModuleOver S :=
  CostructuredArrow.mk (Y := I.left.toRModule) I.hom

/-! ### The construction -/

namespace AnnihilatorConstruction

variable (I : RIdealOver S) (N : RModuleOver S) (Φ : N ⟶ I.asModuleOver)

/-- The sheaf of ideals `θ(J)O_P = f⁻¹(J)` of `O_P`, for `Φ = (f, φ) : N = (P, I) ⟶ M = (X, J)`. -/
def generatedIdeal : RIdeal.{u} := I.left.pullbackIdeal Φ.left.f

/-- The sheaf of ideals `H`: the union of the annihilators of the powers of `θ(J)` in `O_P`.

Definition (p. 127), see `RIdeal.annihilatorUnion`. -/
@[blueprint "def:0.S2-annihilator-union"
  (statement := /-- Let $M=(X,J)$ be an $(\mathcal R/S)$-ideal with $X=(\mathbf X,O_X)$. Let $(N,\Phi)$ be a blowing-up of $M$ in
    the category $\mathcal M(\mathcal R/S)$ with $N=(P,I)$, $P=(\mathbf P,O_P)$, and with $\Phi=(f,\varphi)$,
    $f=(\mathbf f,\theta)$. Let $H$ be the union of the annihilators of $\theta(J)^n$ in $O_P$ for all positive integers
    $n$. (p.~127.) Formalization note (encoding): $\theta(J)^n$ is read through the ideal $\theta(J)O_P$ generated by
    $\theta(J)$; the union is the union of sheaves (locally in some annihilator), given as the family of ideals
    $H(U)\subseteq O_P(U)$. -/)
  (latexEnv := "definition")]
def annihilator : IdealFamily (generatedIdeal I N Φ).X.toSheafedSpace :=
  (generatedIdeal I N Φ).annihilatorFamily

/-- The local-ringed space `P′ = (P′, O_{P′})`: `P′` the support of `O_P/H` and `O_{P′}` the restriction of `O_P/H` to
`P′`.

Definition (p. 127). -/
@[blueprint "def:0.S2-annihilator-support"
  (statement := /-- Let $\mathbf P'$ be the support of $O_P/H$, $O_{P'}$ the restriction of $O_P/H$ to $\mathbf P'$ and
    $P'=(\mathbf P',O_{P'})$. (p.~127.) Formalization note (encoding): $O_P/H$ is the sheafification of
    $U\mapsto O_P(U)/H(U)$, its support is the set of points with non-zero stalk, and the restriction to the
    (non-open) support is the inverse image sheaf; $P'$ is a local-ringed space because its stalks are non-zero quotients
    of the local rings $O_{P,t}$. -/)
  (latexEnv := "definition")]
def support : LocallyRingedSpace.{u} := supportSpace (annihilator I N Φ)

/-- The canonical morphism of local-ringed spaces `P′ ⟶ P`. -/
def supportIncl : support I N Φ ⟶ N.left.X := supportHom (annihilator I N Φ)

/-- The morphism of spaces `f ∘ j : P′ ⟶ X` through which `Φ` induces `Φ′`. -/
def toBase : support I N Φ ⟶ I.left.X := supportIncl I N Φ ≫ Φ.left.f

/-- The sheaf of ideals `I′` in `O_{P′}` generated by the natural image of `θ(J)`: `(f ∘ j)⁻¹(J)` in the notation of
p. 128.

Definition (p. 127). -/
@[blueprint "def:0.S2-annihilator-ideal"
  (statement := /-- Let $I'$ be the sheaf of ideals in $O_{P'}$ which is generated by the natural image of $\theta(J)$.
    (p.~127.) Formalization note (encoding): $I'$ is $(f\circ j)^{-1}(J)=\theta'(J)O_{P'}$, where $j\colon P'\to P$ is
    the canonical morphism and $\theta'$ the ring map of $f\circ j$ (notation of p.~128). -/)
  (latexEnv := "definition")]
def ideal : RIdeal.{u} := I.left.pullbackIdeal (toBase I N Φ)

/-- The `(ℛ/S)`-ideal `N′ = (P′, I′)`, over `S` through `P′ ⟶ P ⟶ S`. -/
def object : RIdealOver S :=
  CostructuredArrow.mk (Y := ideal I N Φ) (supportIncl I N Φ ≫ N.hom)

/-- The natural morphism `Φ′ : (P′, I′) ⟶ (X, J)` induced by `Φ`, a morphism of `(ℛ/S)`-ideals.

> Then Φ induces a natural morphism Φ′: (P′, I′) → (X, J), which is a morphism of (ℛ/S)-ideals. (p. 127)

Definition (p. 127).  Formalization note (encoding): the underlying morphism of spaces is `f ∘ j`; being a morphism of
`(ℛ/S)`-ideals (compatibility with the monomorphisms and with the structure morphisms to `S`) is part of the
construction (`RIdeal.pullbackIdealHom`; the compatibility with `S` is the condition that `Φ` is a morphism of
`(ℛ/S)`-modules). -/
@[blueprint "def:0.S2-annihilator-hom"
  (statement := /-- Then $\Phi$ induces a natural morphism $\Phi'\colon(P',I')\to(X,J)$, which is a morphism of
    $(\mathcal R/S)$-ideals. (p.~127.) Formalization note (encoding): $\Phi'$ is $(f\circ j,\varphi')$ with $\varphi'$ the
    canonical $(f\circ j)$-epimorphism of $J$ onto $\theta'(J)O_{P'}$; it is a morphism over $S$ because $\Phi$ is. -/)
  (latexEnv := "definition")]
def hom : object I N Φ ⟶ I :=
  CostructuredArrow.homMk (RIdeal.pullbackIdealHom I.left (toBase I N Φ)) (by
    have h : Φ.left.f ≫ (I.hom : I.left.X ⟶ S) = (N.hom : N.left.X ⟶ S) := CostructuredArrow.w Φ
    show (supportIncl I N Φ ≫ Φ.left.f) ≫ (I.hom : I.left.X ⟶ S) = supportIncl I N Φ ≫ N.hom
    exact (Category.assoc _ _ _).trans (congrArg (fun g => supportIncl I N Φ ≫ g) h))

end AnnihilatorConstruction

/-- The pair `(N′, Φ′)` of the annihilator construction is a blowing-up of `M` in `𝒥(ℛ/S)`, whenever `(N, Φ)` is a
blowing-up of `M` in `𝓜(ℛ/S)`.

> It can be easily seen that (N′, Φ′) with N′ = (P′, I′) is a blowing-up of M in the category 𝒥(ℛ/S). (p. 127)

Stated without proof ("It can be easily seen", p. 127); not proved here.  Together with the existence of blowing-up in
`𝓜(ℛ/S)` it gives the existence of blowing-up in `𝒥(ℛ/S)` (`IdealExistenceFromModules`, "Thus we obtain the exitence
[sic] theorem ..."), proved from it as `idealExistenceFromModules_of_annihilator`; the same construction is used for
`𝒥*(𝔄l/B)` on p. 128.  Formalization note (encoding): `(N, Φ)` a
blowing-up of the module `M` in `𝓜(ℛ/S)` is `IsBlowingUp (RModuleOver.forget S) Φ`, and the conclusion is
`IsBlowingUp (RIdealOver.toRModule S) Φ′` (blowing-up in `𝒥(ℛ/S)`, with respect to the functor to `𝓜(ℛ)`, as in
`IdealExistenceFromModules`). -/
@[blueprint "prop:0.S2-annihilator-construction-blowing-up"
  (statement := /-- Let $(N,\Phi)$ be a blowing-up of $M=(X,J)$ in the category $\mathcal M(\mathcal R/S)$ and let
    $(N',\Phi')$ with $N'=(P',I')$ be the pair constructed from the annihilators of $\theta(J)^n$. It can be easily
    seen that $(N',\Phi')$ is a blowing-up of $M$ in the category $\mathcal J(\mathcal R/S)$. (p.~127.) Not proved here:
    stated without argument ($\mathcal J(\mathcal R/S)\to\mathcal M(\mathcal R)$ as the functor). -/)
  (latexEnv := "proposition")]
def AnnihilatorConstructionIsBlowingUp : Prop :=
  ∀ (S : LocallyRingedSpace.{u}) (I : RIdealOver S) (N : RModuleOver S) (Φ : N ⟶ I.asModuleOver),
    IsBlowingUp (RModuleOver.forget S) Φ →
      IsBlowingUp (RIdealOver.toRModule S) (AnnihilatorConstruction.hom I N Φ)

/-! ### A step of the deduction of p. 128 -/

namespace AnnihilatorConstruction

/-- Gap filled: a blowing-up in `𝓜(ℛ)` of the underlying module of an `(ℛ/S)`-module `M` that is the target of a morphism
`Φ` of `(ℛ/S)`-modules from `N` is a blowing-up of `M` in `𝓜(ℛ/S)`.  Existence of the factorization: the factorization `χ`
in `𝓜(ℛ)` of a morphism `Ψ` of `(ℛ/S)`-modules through `Φ` is compatible with the structure morphisms, since the structure
morphism of `N` is `f ≫ p` and that of `Q` is `Ψ.f ≫ p`; uniqueness: a morphism of `(ℛ/S)`-modules is determined by its
underlying morphism of `ℛ`-modules.  This is the argument of "In this sense, `𝓜(ℛ/S)` is closed under blowing-up in `𝓜(ℛ)`"
(p. 124), needed because the construction of p. 127 starts from a blowing-up in `𝓜(ℛ/S)`. -/
theorem isBlowingUp_forget {M N : RModuleOver S} (Φ : N ⟶ M)
    (h : IsBlowingUp (𝟭 RModule.{u}) ((RModuleOver.forget S).map Φ)) :
    IsBlowingUp (RModuleOver.forget S) Φ := by
  refine ⟨h.invertible, fun Q Ψ hQ => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨χ, hχ, huniq⟩ := h.universal Q.left Ψ.left hQ
  have hN : Φ.left.f ≫ (M.hom : M.left.X ⟶ S) = (N.hom : N.left.X ⟶ S) := CostructuredArrow.w Φ
  have hQ' : Ψ.left.f ≫ (M.hom : M.left.X ⟶ S) = (Q.hom : Q.left.X ⟶ S) := CostructuredArrow.w Ψ
  have hχf : χ.f ≫ Φ.left.f = Ψ.left.f := congrArg RModule.Hom.f hχ
  refine ⟨CostructuredArrow.homMk χ ?_, ?_, fun Ξ hΞ => ?_⟩
  · show χ.f ≫ (N.hom : N.left.X ⟶ S) = (Q.hom : Q.left.X ⟶ S)
    erw [← hN, ← Category.assoc, hχf]
    exact hQ'
  · apply CostructuredArrow.hom_ext
    exact hχ
  · apply CostructuredArrow.hom_ext
    exact huniq Ξ.left (congrArg CommaMorphism.left hΞ)

end AnnihilatorConstruction

/-- The existence of blowing-up in `𝓜(ℛ/S)` implies the same in `𝒥(ℛ/S)` (p. 127), deduced along the printed
construction.

> However, the existence of blowing-up in the category 𝓜(ℛ/S) implies the same in the category 𝒥(ℛ/S). In fact, let
> M = (X, J) be an (ℛ/S)-ideal ... It can be easily seen that (N′, Φ′) with N′ = (P′, I′) is a blowing-up of M in the
> category 𝒥(ℛ/S). (p. 127)

Printed steps: (1) the ideal `I`, viewed as an `(ℛ/S)`-module, has a blowing-up `(N, Φ)` in `𝓜(ℛ/S)` (the hypothesis of
the statement); (2) the construction of the annihilators of `θ(J)ⁿ` gives `(N′, Φ′)`, a blowing-up of `I` in `𝒥(ℛ/S)`
(`AnnihilatorConstructionIsBlowingUp`: "It can be easily seen", stated without proof, p. 127; assumed, as in the
paper). -/
theorem idealExistenceFromModules_of_annihilator (hann : AnnihilatorConstructionIsBlowingUp.{u}) :
    IdealExistenceFromModules.{u} := by
  intro S hM I
  -- (1) a blowing-up `(N, Φ)` of `I`, viewed as an `(ℛ/S)`-module, in `𝓜(ℛ/S)`.
  obtain ⟨N, Φ, hΦ⟩ := hM I.asModuleOver
  -- (2) the construction of p. 127 and its claim.
  exact ⟨_, _, hann S I N Φ hΦ⟩

end Hironaka

end
